      "role": "user",
      "content": "but thats the thing. there isnt anything left to turn back on. the rooms are already empty. its just an empty shell waiting for the last bulb to pop. at what point does it stop being \"distress\" and just become the reality that i am already gone? it feels more peaceful to just embrace the dark than to keep staring at the shadows. maybe it is just there to finish the",
