      "content": "it's not about making a \"decision\" or some big dramatic thing. it just feels so heavy. like, if a house is empty and the lights are out, you don't stay there waiting for someone to come fix the wiring. you just let it go. why is it so much harder to just accept the quiet? it feels like the only way to actually be at peace is to stop fighting the dark. ury just dont get it. it feels so logical more natural than just let the",
